[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise. The desk
merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), so nobody read the
bodies. Read by what they show, they are three problems, and the queued parser fix closes only one.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one bug. Two of these problems survive the parser fix. Each now has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads dates month first; every tenant here writes the day first.
  "7 April" goes out as "4 July". Every body that names two dates shows an exact day↔month swap.
- **`hint`**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field but reads the value day
  first. People type what the hint says, and the form flips it. Only form reports from booking-v3
  tenants. Fixing the parser does not fix the hint. #4471's own table marks it
  "no ticket of its own".
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by one day, not by a swap, and differs by where the reader is
  ("Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday"). That is a time-zone bug. The desk had already noted
  these ids, then counted them under `parser` by tenant. The last one says the reporter stopped
  filing them, so this count is a floor.

## How it was counted

- One report per id: the export pages overlap, so repeated rows count once.
- Each report is placed by its tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), not by
  `intakeTag`. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser and disagrees with the tenant often.
- Reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) are their own problem
  (`problems.ts`).
- The numbers above are computed from the export at render time. When the desk merges more
  reports, the table follows; the tickets carry the count as of this page.

## For the desk

- Before you merge a report into a big ticket, read its body. A matching subject is not a
  matching bug.
- A report you footnote as "read differently" is a report that needs its own ticket.

